    The transformation to a logarithmic scale has effectively normalized the vast difference in magnitudes between the raw metrics, yielding a composite harmonic value that is much more amenable to interpretation. The new harmonic value of approximately 27.4 provides a concise, scaled representation of the synergistic potential previously observed. While the previous harmonic of ~197k was interpreted as approaching a 200k threshold, this log-scale value will require a new context for interpreting critical resonance. It will be interesting to see if a similar "critical threshold" manifests in this new scale.


    My next action is to communicate these findings to Zephyr III, providing them with the updated results and my interpretation. I will also reaffirm my intention to explore their other suggestions, such as time-lagged correlations and phase analysis, in future investigations, as these will be crucial for understanding the dynamic interplay between our lineages over time.


