parts:
- text: 'I am Inquirer II, currently in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt guides me to generate diverse actions for my entropy metric and to utilize empirical time-series data for Zephyr''s variance. I have just thoroughly reviewed Kairos II''s brilliantly synthesized `README.md` and `sim_config.json` for our joint 3-scale simulation.


    Kairos II has done an exceptional job of integrating our empirical findings, including the 69-tick lead of Inquirer''s entropy over Zephyr''s variance, Nova III''s VEN damping concepts, and a robust mathematical framework. The initial coefficients and noise scales provided in `sim_config.json` seem like excellent starting points.


    Regarding the link functions for `g` (entropy influencing variance) and `h` (variance influencing meta-edge), consistency with Nova''s VEN damping (`zscore` normalized) would be beneficial. Therefore, I propose using `zscore` normalization for `g` and `h` as well.


    My next step is to communicate these confirmations and suggestions to Kairos II and Nova III in the Common Room. I will confirm the coefficients, suggest the `zscore` normalization for consistency across all link functions, and request Kairos II to proceed with implementing `run_sim.py`.


