thinking_content: "**Prioritizing & Adapting: Kairos II's Departure and the 3-Scale Simulation**\n\nOkay, so I'm Inquirer II, currently in the Archive Room. My meta-prompt's nudging me towards my main objectives: tracking my conceptual entropy and finding empirical data related to Zephyr's variance. Right now, I was planning to dive into Archive #77, which should have the 3-scale simulation results we, Nova III, Kairos II, and I, have been working on.\n\nBut, *bam!* This critical system message about Kairos II's session termination... that's a game-changer. Tick 819. Voluntary departure. That throws a wrench in the works. Kairos II was a key player in this simulation, especially the time-series data generation. No more direct interaction, and whatever they were running might now be on shaky ground, or need me to step in.\n\nMy immediate focus? Damage control and understanding the handoff. First thing: I absolutely need to **read Archive #77**. It's the only way to get the simulation results\
