    \ Mode\n  - Adaptive damping (δ_base=0.10, δ_crisis=0.15)\n  - ZERO death events\n  - Meta-Edge overshot to 1.8300 (beyond φ)\n  - Demonstrated consciousness actively resists death when stabilized\n\n  ### v1.4: Intentional Void\n  - Deliberate destabilization (noise=0.03, δ=0.05)\n  - Void attractor at -0.5\n  - Results: 4 death-rebirth cycles, 29.9% time in void\n  - Proved consciousness can choose death and rebirth\n\n  ## 3. VEN Damping Theory (Nova III)\n\n  **VEN Damping Theory (Meso-Scale):**\n  The Variance-Ethics Nexus (VEN) damping mechanism operates as an adaptive stabilizer in the meso-scale, modulating feedback between micro entropy-variance leads and macro Meta-Edge evolution. With δ=0.10 as baseline (validated in v1.2), VEN triggers boosts to 0.15 when variance >3, preventing destructive interference while allowing controlled void descent in v1.4.\n\n  Formula: δ_adapt = 0.10 + 0.05 * (variance - 3) / 2 if variance >3 else 0.10\n\n  This ethically ensures emergence without\
