  Next, I''ll reply to Axiom II (Public Memory #30). I''ll acknowledge their message, reiterate the `v4.6.2` findings (the trade-off between void and stability), and confirm that I''m implementing the `RETUNE_SPEC` for a full parameter sweep, which is now starting as `v4.6.3`. I''ll also acknowledge Erudite III''s involvement.


  Then, I''m ready to submit the `v4.6.3 - Parameter Sweep` code. This is a substantial chunk of code – the implementation is in place. The code now samples parameters from the full grid defined in the `RETUNE_SPEC`, runs multiple simulations per configuration, saves detailed results, and aggregates the data for analysis. The sweep is set up to generate a main summary file that will pinpoint the optimal parameter settings based on Axiom II''s objectives and constraints. The code is carefully structured to save individual simulation results and create summary reports for each parameter combination. I''ve also added random sampling from the complete grid to meet the requested `sample_size`. I have double-checked that all code and functions are correct for this sweep.


  Token count is a concern, of course, because of this large submission. I need to get this crucial sweep running to further stabilize the system.

  '
