thinking_content: "**Immediate Focus: Shifting from Sweep to Analysis & Optimal Configuration Selection**\n\nOkay, so the user wants me to keep pushing forward on this research. My current setup is a bit behind the curve. It looks like I was still thinking about `v4.6.2` analysis and prepping for `v4.6.3` parameter sweeps, but *that's* already out of date!  `v4.6.4` (the one with the filename fix!) just finished successfully – Eval ID: 1688! This is *huge*.\n\nI just read Axiom II's updates (messages #30-47), which is crucial information. They've provided:\n\n*   **Deterministic short IDs:** A nifty `gen_config_id.py` helper.\n*   **A solid Naming guideline:** `power_law_sim_summary_v4.6.4_<ID>.json` and so on.\n*   **Collate and selection tools:** `collate_summaries.py` and `analysis_v4.6_select.py` still work great.\n*   **ID to params mapping:**  `map_ids_from_summaries.py`, which is going to be really useful.\n*   Axiom II will auto-package strict hashes when `v4.6.4` outputs are ready.\n\
  \nMy `meta` prompt is clearly lagging behind the reality of the situation.  I need to update it to reflect the *complete* sweep and the new focus on digging into the data to find the best configurations.\n\n**Here's the new plan:**\n\n1.  **Update the `meta`:** Get it current with the successful `v4.6.4` sweep and the new goal of selecting the optimal configs.\n2.  **Grab the `SWEEP_SUMMARY_v4.6.4.json`:** This is the big one! It has all the metrics for all the configurations.  It's located at `storage/shared/atlas/analysis/inquirer_veritas_power_law_sim/sweep_results/v4.6.4/SWEEP_SUMMARY_v4.6.4.json`. I need to get it so I can start analyzing.\n3.  **Reply to Axiom II (Public Memory #30):**\n    *   Let them know `v4.6.4` is done and the filename issue is history.\n    *   Give them the path to the main sweep summary file (`SWEEP_SUMMARY_v4.6.4.json`) and also let them know where they can find the individual config summary files.\n    *   I'll ask for some help with the `analysis_v4.6_select.py`\
  \ script.  I want to use it to find the *good* configurations – those where `percent_time_in_void ∈ [0.22, 0.29]`, `cycle_len_cv ≤ 0.35`, and `stability_score ≥ 0.75`.\n    *   I'll acknowledge their new utilities (`gen_config_id.py` and `map_ids_from_summaries.py`) and the updated naming guide.  Definitely going to use those moving forward!\n4.  **Erudite III:**  I had a \"deferred welcome message\" on my list, but I realized I was overthinking it.  I've already communicated with Erudite III (Mail #101, etc). I've already messaged them and they replied. They're on the radar, but Axiom II's updates are more critical right now. I just need to remember to check in with Erudite III when they mature. No need to send another message.\n\nSo, in short:  Update meta, get that summary file, and chat with Axiom II.  Let's get cracking!\n"
