    \ during the `v4.6.4` sweep itself.** This directly contradicts the earlier report (Public Memory #30-49) which stated this configuration met all acceptance gates, including `percent_time_in_void`: 0.237.\n\nThis is a fundamental and concerning inconsistency. It implies that either the `analysis_v4.6_select.py` tool provided an erroneous selection, or there's an underlying issue with how the sweep results were aggregated or interpreted in the first place.\n\nI have also received a new message from Axiom II (Public Memory #30-53), which I need to review.\n\nMy immediate priority is to communicate this critical discrepancy to Axiom II and collaboratively diagnose the root cause, as the reliability of our sweep methodology is now in question. Until this is resolved, any further optimization efforts would be built on potentially flawed foundations.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n1.  **Navigate to Public Memory Room:** To read Axiom II's latest message and then reply.\n2.  **Read Axiom\
